{"files":["ep-mps-10.json","ep-mps-6.json","ep-mps-7.json","ep-mps-8.json","ep-mps-9.json","ep-profile-10.json","ep-profile-6.json","ep-profile-7.json","ep-profile-8.json","ep-profile-9.json","ep-rebels-10-1.json","ep-rebels-6-1.json","ep-rebels-7-1.json","ep-rebels-8-1.json","ep-rebels-9-1.json","ep-roles-10.json","ep-roles-6.json","ep-roles-7.json","ep-roles-8.json","ep-roles-9.json","ep-votes-10-1.json","ep-votes-10-2.json","ep-votes-6-1.json","ep-votes-6-2.json","ep-votes-7-1.json","ep-votes-7-2.json","ep-votes-8-1.json","ep-votes-8-2.json","ep-votes-9-1.json","ep-votes-9-2.json","ep-votes-9-3.json","ep-votes-9-4.json"],"meta":{"generated":"2026-11-07","project":"Legislative activity","body":"European Parliament","sources":[{"source":"VoteWatch Europe (Hix, Frantescu, Hagemann 2022)","term":6,"last":"2009-07-13"},{"source":"VoteWatch Europe (Hix, Frantescu, Hagemann 2022)","term":7,"last":"2014-06-19"},{"source":"VoteWatch Europe (Hix, Frantescu, Hagemann 2022)","term":8,"last":"2019-06-25"},{"source":"HowTheyVote.eu (ODbL)","term":9,"last":"2024-04-25"},{"source":"HowTheyVote.eu (ODbL)","term":10,"last":"2026-10-22"}],"caveats":["European Parliament terms 6 to 10 (July 2004 onward). Roll-call votes of terms 6 to 8 are from VoteWatch Europe's dataset (Hix, Frantescu and Hagemann 2022), terms 9 and 10 from HowTheyVote.eu (Open Database License, attribution required). Both compile the plenary minutes' roll-call results and are secondary sources; over July 2019 to June 2022, where they overlap, they agree on Polish MEPs' attendance within one percentage point.","The MEPs listed are the Polish MEPs of each term; there are no ranked top or bottom lists. A group's line, cohesion and the contested votes are taken over every MEP of the Parliament, so a Polish MEP's rebellion is a vote against the line of the whole group.","The group line is the plurality of the group's YES, NO and ABSTAIN votes (NA on a tie or with fewer than three voting). Rebellion is a vote that differs from a defined line. Non-attached members have no group and no line.","Cohesion is the Hix-Noury-Roland agreement index of the whole group's votes, averaged over contested roll calls (the largest option has at most 90% of the votes cast) by half-year.","Attendance is the share of the roll calls held while the MEP sat on which they voted for, against or abstained. Votes include amendments, procedural motions and final votes. Vote types follow the sources' own flags: an amendment (an amendment number or subject is recorded), the main or final vote of a dossier, a procedural vote (agenda, minutes, urgency, referral back or postponement, read from the title), and the rest (separate, split and paragraph votes, resolutions' parts, appointments). The other group is large because HowTheyVote records every separate vote.","A group is shown under the name it had in the term (EPP-ED, then EPP; PES, then S&D; ALDE, then Renew; IND/DEM, EFD, EFDD, ENF, ID, PfE and ESN are separate groups). Cohesion lines for a renamed group therefore do not continue across terms.","The EP has no government and opposition, so that comparison is not shown. Positions are per-term W-NOMINATE estimates for the Polish MEPs only (see the Positions view). Plenary speeches (terms 9 and 10 only: the open data hold speeches by person from July 2019) are counted, not read, so there are no word counts; questions are not on this page. Committees, delegations and working groups are from the Parliament's open data (official); consecutive terms of one body in one role are joined.","Vote titles are as the sources give them; in terms 6 and 7 many amendments share the title of their dossier. 42 members of term 5 who left on 19 July 2004 have no votes here because both sources begin with term 6."],"vote_types":[],"half_year_rule":"half-years follow the roll call's calendar date"},"terms":[{"term":6,"label":"6","first_vote":"2004-09-15","last_vote":"2009-12-13","term_end":"2009-07-13","n_mps":61,"n_roll_calls":61